		out << setw(8) << table.row[i];
		for (unsigned int j = 0; j < table.col.size(); j++) {
			rule cell = table.rules[i * table.col.size() + j];
			if (cell.right.empty()) {
				out << setw(12) << " ";//空单元格代表分析到此处即出错
				continue;
			}
			//借助字符串流把产生式整体作为一个单元格输出，宽度才不会被打乱
			ostringstream cell_text;
			cell_text << cell;
			out << setw(12) << cell_text.str();
		}
		out << endl;
	}
	out << right;//恢复默认的对齐方式，避免影响后面的输出
	return out;
}
```

Clause map: *"formatted grid"* — `setw` throughout, matching the lexer's `setw(8)/setw(12)` token table. *"row and column headers"* — the `setw(8) << " "` corner then `col[j]` across the top, `row[i]` down the left. The `ostringstream` matters: `out << setw(12) << cell` would apply the width to the *first* insertion inside `operator<<(rule)` (the `left` char) and shred the grid — the production has to be stringified first. `left`/`right` are set and restored so the stream is handed back in its default state.

